      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CASTERTON (10) is a progressive colt from a premier Victorian yard. Made it two wins in a row when he worked but was too good by 8.6m in his heat at this circuit and distance last week. Draws on the back row but scored from this barrier two back at Kilmore so looks the one to beat. RANKINE (8) is hard to knock having taken his unbeaten run to three when coming from this barrier for a 2m win in his heat last week. He is a big chance to keep the unblemished record intact. ONE AUSSIE (7) was a solid second behind CASTERTON after working last start and returns to the front row, albeit wide. Can feature along with JADES REASON (1) who chased RANKINE as runner-up last week and draws to enjoy the favours.",
